        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4b9c29ff-a47e-51cf-913e-9006e91593cc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lindka Cierach, Helen Mirren, Sarah Ferguson, Prince Andrew, Lady Victoria Hervey, Cherie Blair, Queen Elizabeth II\n- Organizations: British Royal Family, European Royal Families, Royal Shakespeare Company\n- Products: Wedding dress of Sarah Ferguson, The Queen\n- Concepts: Triple Crown of Acting, Academy Award for Best Actress\n\nFacts:\n- In 1967, Helen Mirren began her acting career with the Royal Shakespeare Company.\n- Helen Mirren is one of the few performers to achieve the Triple Crown of Acting.\n- In 2007, Helen Mirren won the Academy Award for Best Actress for playing Queen Elizabeth II in The Queen after receiving two previous nominations.\n- Lindka Cierach's notable clients include members of British and European Royal Families, Helen Mirren, Lady Victoria Hervey, and Cherie Blair.\n- Lindka Cierach designed Sarah Ferguson's wedding dress.\n- The beadwork on Sarah Ferguson's wedding dress included hearts for romance, anchors and waves for Prince Andrew's sailing background, and bumblebees and thistles from Sarah Ferguson's family crest.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "82336dcf-4083-5b30-9a0f-8a37e23d9557",
        "text": "Page: Lindka Cierach. Sentence: Notable clients include members of British and European Royal Families, Helen Mirren, Lady Victoria Hervey and Cherie Blair among others.\nPage: Helen Mirren. Sentence: Mirren began her acting career with the Royal Shakespeare Company in 1967, and is one of the few performers who have achieved the Triple Crown of Acting, having won the Academy Award for Best Actress in 2007, after two previous nominations, for her performance as Queen Elizabeth II in \"The Queen\".\nPage: Wedding dress of Sarah Ferguson. Sentence: Designed by Lindka Cierach, the beadwork incorporated various symbols including hearts representing romance, anchors and waves representing Prince Andrew's sailing background and bumblebees and thistles, which were taken from Sarah Ferguson's family crest.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
